  "title": "The Least Frobenius Alexander Quandle Isogeny-Detection Prime over F_5",
  "batch_label": "61",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Using the Frobenius Alexander quandle convention and the quandle-isomorphism/Frobenius-similarity equivalence of arXiv:2609.02278v1, the least rational prime ell != 5 such that, uniformly for all elliptic curves A,B over F_5, isomorphic quandles Q(A[ell],pi_A,ell) and Q(B[ell],pi_B,ell) force A and B to be F_5-isogenous is ell=11. Uniform sufficiency holds at 11. The smaller eligible primes all fail: at ell=2 use y^2=x^3+3x and y^2=x^3+1; at ell=3 use y^2=x^3+3x+2 and y^2=x^3+4x; at ell=7 use y^2=x^3+3x and y^2=x^3+4x+2. In each pair the curves are nonsingular and nonisogenous, while their torsion Frobenius operators have the same explicitly certified rational canonical form.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
